Package: lexsync
Type: Package
Title: Lexical Optimisation and Hardware-Timed Experiment Generation
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Pablo", "Bernabeu", email = "pcbernabeu@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1083-2460"))
Description: A cross-platform toolkit for lexical-corpus access (bundled
    English, Spanish and Mandarin lexica and a registry of citable corpora),
    the matching of stimuli on several dimensions at once, deterministic
    pseudoword generation, counterbalancing and the automated generation of
    experiments from a declarative trial-event model, for 'PsychoPy',
    'OpenSesame' and the browser ('jsPsych'). The laboratory targets send
    electroencephalography onset triggers on the screen refresh that shows the
    stimulus. Several paradigms are supported (factorial word contrasts, lexical
    decision, priming, self-paced reading and cued categorisation), and each
    design is accompanied by a materials datasheet, readable by machines and
    people, for reproducibility. A 'Python' package of the same name has the
    same structure and functions.
